  "slug": "protein-model-93eb",
  "summary": "Seven preprints add dynamics, 3D context, reference modeling or structure-derived profiles to sequence models for variant, PTM, kcat and design tasks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is specializing sequence representations for defined prediction tasks by supplying task-relevant information that generic embeddings lack. DynamicsPLM adds molecular dynamics heads to a 35M-parameter model for zero-shot variant effect prediction. HieraPTM combines sequence, language model and 3D structure features to progress from PTM site recognition to functional phosphosite prediction. EnzRef models reactants and products separately against a frozen protein language model to predict kcat. Adjacent structure-focused work follows a related logic: FoldMapper uses structure-derived evolutionary profiles for inverse folding, MANTA separates geometric prior estimation from coordinate generation for disordered ensembles, and AbPoolRank selects among mixed antibody-antigen prediction pools (58.0% Success@1). MXfold2 adds chemical probing supervision for RNA secondary structure. These are not all language-model adapters, but they share task-specific augmentation of sequence-only inputs.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
